# `#App.Every(cron:)` runs on one server at a time across replicas, and a
# missed run runs once at start-up. Two replicas of the fixture's app, each
# with its own handle on the same store, start together; the latest leap day
# is a run no server made, so it runs at start-up. The store records the run
# in the run's transaction (`__jet_schedules`), so it counts once and the
# other replica drops it. Run again, as after a restart, the store has the
# run already, and the count stays 1. A cron line that doesn't parse, and a
# schedule method that takes a parameter, are E2805 at the mount.
fixture: ScheduleRunsOnceAcrossReplicas.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step start: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "leap day runs: 1\n"
step restart: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "leap day runs: 1\n"

step: jet check probes/bad_schedule.jet
exit: nonzero
stderr: ~ "`0 8 * *` is not a cron line: it has 4 fields, not 5" # the four-field line
stderr: ~ "bad_schedule.jet:11:" # at its marker's line
stderr: ~ "Schedule method `remind` needs read-only self, no other parameters and a concrete signature" # the schedule with a parameter
stderr: ~ "bad_schedule.jet:13:" # at its marker's line
stderr: ~ "2 problems found" # one per schedule
